          "create_time": 1793939233.018,
          "update_time": 1793939256.127,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The tradeoff is **which part of the physics we explain, and which part we supply externally**.\n\n**Direct Newman avenue:** we prepare the canonical radial source \\(F_\\lambda(v)=e^{\\lambda v^2}\\Phi(v)\\), then observe its signed Fourier amplitude, which gives \\(H_\\lambda\\) exactly. This keeps Newman evolution central. But the free cylinder Hamiltonian differentiates in position; Newman evolution multiplies by \\(v^2\\). A physical controller producing that multiplication would be an added model choice. Increasing \\(\\lambda\\) also requires unbounded gain on the unrestricted field space, although the canonical source itself remains well defined.\n\n**Free-Hamiltonian auxiliary avenue:** we prepare the source once and evolve it by the cylinder’s natural proper-time heat operator. The proposed readout is\n\\[\n\\mathcal O_{\\lambda,\\tau}(k)\n=e^{-\\tau k^2}\\frac{Q_1(\\pi+4\\tau)}{Q_1(\\pi)}\\,H_\\lambda(k).\n\\]\nHere \\(\\tau\\) is proper time and \\(\\lambda\\) remains an independent preparation parameter. This gives a cleaner role to the existing Hamiltonian and retains every angular channel. Its limitation is substantial: the multiplier never vanishes, so the evolution preserves existing zeros and multiplicities. Recovering \\(H\\) also amplifies high-frequency errors. It supplies a physical response interpretation, with no present improvement in collision control.\n\n**Both still require the same supplied ingredient:** imprinting the angular-response scan as a position-dependent radial source. Translation invariance of the free cylinder does not explain the rule \\(\\beta(v)=\\pi e^{4v}\\).\n\nMy tentative preference was the auxiliary avenue as a modest first interpretation. But if your priority is explaining where the canonical source or Newman clock comes from intrinsically, that would be too modest: we should retain that precise missing construction instead of freezing a heat-response exercise. No E02 request has been frozen yet."
            ]
          },
